.TH KSMBD.SELFTEST "8" "" "ksmbd-tools @ksmbd_tools_version@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ksmbd.selftest \- run self-tests for ksmbd kernel server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ksmbd.selftest
\-\-init
.br
.B ksmbd.selftest
\-\-xfstests
.br
.B ksmbd.selftest
\-\-smbtorture
.br
.B ksmbd.selftest
\-\-unit
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBksmbd.selftest\fR runs self-tests for the \fBksmbd\fR kernel server.
It automates the setup and execution of test suites against a local ksmbd instance, similar to the Linux kernel tools/kselftest framework.
\fBksmbd.selftest\fR uses the bundled \fBksmbd.selftest.conf\fR configuration file, handles user creation, daemon startup, test execution, and cleanup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-init\fR
Install dependencies and build test tools (xfsprogs, smbtorture) into \fB/opt/ksmbd\-selftest\fR.
Supports Debian/Ubuntu (apt-get) and RHEL/Fedora (dnf).
Only needs to be run once per machine.
.TP
\fB\-\-xfstests\fR
Run xfstests (filesystem-level tests via CIFS mount).
Must be run from the xfsprogs-dev build directory containing the \fB./check\fR script.
Generates a \fBlocal.config\fR for xfstests per the Samba xfstesting-cifs wiki.
.TP
\fB\-\-smbtorture\fR
Run Samba smbtorture (SMB2 protocol-level tests).
Requires \fBsmbtorture\fR to be in \fBPATH\fR.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Output version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display this help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB@sysconfdir@/ksmbd/ksmbd.selftest.conf\fR
Configuration file defining test shares used by \fBksmbd.selftest\fR.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
The exit status is 0 on success and 1 on failure.
